    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"soft landing\" sounds like a very optimistic way of putting it. if we look at the geopolitical reality—the heavy reliance on certain countries for these minerals and the massive subsidies needed to keep renewables competitive—it looks more like a forced economic experiment. wouldn't you say the arguments that prioritize decarbonization over energy security and low costs are actually fundamentally flawed, rather than just \"logistical risks\"?",
